  "body": "The reference implementation currently parses `C|` against `file://host/dir/file` as `file://host/dir/C|`. \r\n\r\nAgainst the same base URL, \r\n* `C|` is parsed as `file://host/dir/C|` \r\n* `C|#` is parsed as `file:///C:#`\r\n* `C|?` is parsed as `file:///C:?`\r\n* `C|/` is parsed as `file:///C:/`\r\n* `/C|` is parsed as `file:///C:`\r\n* etc,\r\n\r\nI am not (yet) sure if this is according to the current specification or an issue with the reference implementation. I would propose changing this behaviour to have `C|` yield `file:///C:`.  ",
